All MUST SHOW items check out: slim identity bar with `← demo` exit to the chain, truncated hash, `Partial` badge and `block 101`; four stepping groups covering both directions, scrubber, `128 / 1315` readout and the FETCHING/OPENING/POSITIONING rail; Code pane with the current position unmistakable on line 32; CALL TRACE / EVENT LOG as one tabbed region with Call Trace open and seven frames; Values a separate pane below the tabs, not a third tab; Transaction pane whose first row is `DATA` with the `Synthetic demo data` badge and the producer's own sentences. No spinner, no empty pane, no prose band above the panes, no full-width pane row, no provenance band. Register is right. The new bottom fades work — the Transaction pane's EXECUTIONS sentence fades mid-line rather than stopping flat.

The weakest element is the phase rail, identity bar x≈958-1205, and yes it is still the rail — but for a reason specific to 1440. The honest state is not readable here because the words that name its subject are dropped at this width. At 1920 the bar reads `…scrubber — Engine loading — 18 MB — 128 / 1315 — [FETCHING|OPENING|POSITIONING]`. At 1440 that phrase is the first thing responsive layout discards: the gap between the scrubber (ends x≈833) and the readout (x≈855) is empty. What remains is three unlabelled chips. Nothing on this page contains the word "engine". So the rail asserts a phase about an object the page never names, and its terminal chip is POSITIONING — the exact thing the panes visibly already did: line 32 highlighted, frame six selected, values at step N, 128 / 1315. The reader is handed two true facts with the noun that separates them deleted, and the two available readings are both wrong — either the rail is stale, or the populated panes are a skeleton. The inert controls cannot rescue it: their glyph ink is #565656, byte-identical to the not-yet-reached `OPENING` and `POSITIONING` chips 300px to the right, so the disabled cue and the "hasn't happened yet" cue are the same grey. I accept the HONEST adjudication and am not re-filing the P1 — the information is true; what fails is that at this viewport it is carried entirely by three unlabelled chips. Restore `Engine loading — 18 MB` at laptop width, or label the rail.

